WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:02.568
-President Trump
spent the weekend

00:00:02.568 --> 00:00:04.570
attacking the Democrats
running for president

00:00:04.570 --> 00:00:06.672
and the Democrats investigating
him in Congress.

00:00:06.672 --> 00:00:08.574
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:08.574 --> 00:00:12.812
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.812 --> 00:00:14.647
For the first two years
of his presidency,

00:00:14.647 --> 00:00:17.416
Trump enjoyed unified Republican
power in Washington.

00:00:17.416 --> 00:00:19.585
But after the blue wave election
in November,

00:00:19.585 --> 00:00:21.688
Trump is besieged by Democrats
on all sides,

00:00:21.688 --> 00:00:23.956
from the Democrats
investigating him in Congress

00:00:23.956 --> 00:00:25.858
to the Democrats
running for president.

00:00:25.858 --> 00:00:27.727
In fact, tonight,
after we taped this,

00:00:27.727 --> 00:00:29.562
Trump held a rally
in El Paso, Texas,

00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:30.930
to argue for his border wall.

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:33.533
Now, normally,
when Trump holds these rallies,

00:00:33.533 --> 00:00:36.302
he gets the full undivided
attention of the media

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:37.670
and the political world.

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:40.239
But tonight he had to deal with
a rival rally

00:00:40.239 --> 00:00:41.708
held by a popular Democrat

00:00:41.708 --> 00:00:44.009
in a march organized by
local activists.

00:00:44.009 --> 00:00:47.146
-Dueling rallies at the Mexico
border tonight in El Paso.

00:00:47.146 --> 00:00:50.383
President Trump and rising
Democratic star Beto O'Rourke

00:00:50.383 --> 00:00:52.885
both in the West Texas city
tonight.

00:00:52.885 --> 00:00:55.354
O'Rourke plans to lead
a one-mile march celebrating

00:00:55.354 --> 00:00:57.891
the culture, history,
and diversity of the region.

00:00:57.891 --> 00:01:00.426
His speech afterward
timed to coincide with

00:01:00.426 --> 00:01:03.463
the President's rally
at the El Paso County Coliseum.

00:01:03.463 --> 00:01:05.664
-Amazing. Not only are
they holding a rally

00:01:05.664 --> 00:01:08.167
at the same time, but they're
also holding a march.

00:01:08.167 --> 00:01:10.904
There's no better way to troll
Trump than with exercise.

00:01:10.904 --> 00:01:12.371
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.371 --> 00:01:13.406
What's Trump gonna do?

00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:15.241
Chase after the marchers
in his golf cart?

00:01:15.241 --> 00:01:20.179
"Slow down. This thing is
running low on batteries."

00:01:20.179 --> 00:01:22.748
Meanwhile, over the weekend,
two more Democrats announced

00:01:22.748 --> 00:01:24.083
their presidential campaigns,

00:01:24.083 --> 00:01:26.752
adding to what is
an already historic number

00:01:26.752 --> 00:01:28.054
of women in the field.

00:01:28.054 --> 00:01:30.389
On Sunday, Minnesota Senator
Amy Klobuchar

00:01:30.389 --> 00:01:31.690
announced her campaign,

00:01:31.690 --> 00:01:34.327
and she did it the most
Minnesota way possible --

00:01:34.327 --> 00:01:35.328
covered in snow.

00:01:35.328 --> 00:01:39.231
-Now, we don't let a little snow
stop us.

00:01:39.231 --> 00:01:42.835
We don't let a little cold
stop us.

00:01:42.835 --> 00:01:45.104
Like, are you guys even cold?

00:01:45.104 --> 00:01:51.243
So let's join together, as one
nation, indivisible, under God,

00:01:51.243 --> 00:01:54.146
and pursue the good.

00:01:54.146 --> 00:01:58.051
-I promise I will vote for you
if you go inside!

00:01:58.051 --> 00:01:59.251
[ Laughter ]

00:01:59.251 --> 00:02:00.519
Look at all that snow.

00:02:00.519 --> 00:02:02.488
Who's gonna be your
running mate?

00:02:02.488 --> 00:02:03.456
Marge Gunderson?

00:02:03.456 --> 00:02:05.225
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.225 --> 00:02:10.029
Is she in Minnesota
or north of the wall?

00:02:10.029 --> 00:02:11.797
And, of course,
after her announcement,

00:02:11.797 --> 00:02:14.333
Trump couldn't help but take
a shot at Klobuchar on Twitter.

00:02:14.333 --> 00:02:16.869
And in doing so, he once again
revealed that he doesn't know

00:02:16.869 --> 00:02:19.038
the difference between weather
and climate change.

00:02:19.038 --> 00:02:21.240
-President Trump not impressed,
tweeting,

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:22.575
"Well, it happened again.

00:02:22.575 --> 00:02:25.545
Amy Klobuchar announced that she
is running for president,

00:02:25.545 --> 00:02:27.780
talking proudly of fighting
global warming

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.916
while standing in
a virtual blizzard of

00:02:29.916 --> 00:02:31.217
snow, ice,
and freezing temperatures.

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:32.652
Bad timing.

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:37.257
By the end of her speech, she
looked like a snowman or woman."

00:02:37.257 --> 00:02:38.891
-Why do we have to
keep explaining to

00:02:38.891 --> 00:02:40.426
the President of
the United States

00:02:40.426 --> 00:02:42.895
that weather and climate
are two different things?

00:02:42.895 --> 00:02:44.196
We live in a country where

00:02:44.196 --> 00:02:46.199
science teachers
have to tell their students,

00:02:46.199 --> 00:02:48.501
"I don't care
what the President said."

00:02:48.501 --> 00:02:50.102
Not to mention history teachers,

00:02:50.102 --> 00:02:51.970
English teachers
and P.E. teachers.

00:02:51.970 --> 00:03:00.045
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:00.045 --> 00:03:02.048
"I don't care what he said,
Timmy.

00:03:02.048 --> 00:03:03.850
Sit-ups are not fake news."

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:04.851
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.851 --> 00:03:06.785
Shouldn't have to live
like this.

00:03:06.785 --> 00:03:09.054
It's like if a kid pees
his pants when he's 3,

00:03:09.054 --> 00:03:10.456
it's understandable.

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:14.894
But if he does it when he's 30,
you put him in an Uber.

00:03:14.894 --> 00:03:17.796
To explain this one more time,
just because it snows once

00:03:17.796 --> 00:03:20.533
doesn't negate
long-term climate trends

00:03:20.533 --> 00:03:22.602
caused by the burning of
fossil fuels.

00:03:22.602 --> 00:03:24.003
It's kind of like this.

00:03:24.003 --> 00:03:26.872
When your hair looks normal once
in a while, that's weather.

00:03:26.872 --> 00:03:29.909
But most of the time it looks
like this, and that's climate.

00:03:29.909 --> 00:03:31.543
[ Laughter ]

00:03:31.543 --> 00:03:34.113
Now, Klobuchar's announcement
came just a day after

00:03:34.113 --> 00:03:35.815
Massachusetts Senator
Elizabeth Warren

00:03:35.815 --> 00:03:37.783
officially threw her hat
in the ring, as well.

00:03:37.783 --> 00:03:39.652
And rather than focus
exclusively on Trump,

00:03:39.652 --> 00:03:42.255
Warren argued that Trump is just
the product of a broken system.

00:03:42.255 --> 00:03:47.126
-The man in the White House is
not the cause of what is broken.

00:03:47.126 --> 00:03:51.130
He is just the latest
and most extreme symptom

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:54.033
of what's gone wrong in America.

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:57.035
-Basically what she is saying is
Trump himself isn't the disease.

00:03:57.035 --> 00:03:58.137
He's just the symptom.

00:03:58.137 --> 00:03:59.939
Actually, he's
a bunch of symptoms.

00:03:59.939 --> 00:04:01.741
He's basically everything
you'd see

00:04:01.741 --> 00:04:03.109
on the back of a pill bottle.

00:04:03.109 --> 00:04:06.846
May cause inflammation,
excessive sweating, hair loss,

00:04:06.846 --> 00:04:10.216
discoloration of the skin,
and dryness of the mouth.

00:04:10.216 --> 00:04:14.087
-10,000 known
or suspes-- gang members.

00:04:14.087 --> 00:04:17.757
Every single car out there,
even the really expenses ones,

00:04:17.757 --> 00:04:20.526
God bless the United Shtates.

00:04:20.526 --> 00:04:21.994
[ Laughter ]

00:04:21.994 --> 00:04:25.932
-"Oh, is it time for my speech?
Quick. Give me a glass of sand."

00:04:25.932 --> 00:04:30.936
[ Laughter ]

00:04:30.936 --> 00:04:32.805
Now, Warren isn't alone
among Democrats

00:04:32.805 --> 00:04:35.274
in wanting to focus on policy
and on the specific ways

00:04:35.274 --> 00:04:37.442
in which the system
has failed working people.

00:04:37.442 --> 00:04:40.412
The entire Democratic Party's
messaging in the midterms

00:04:40.412 --> 00:04:41.614
was focused on issues

00:04:41.614 --> 00:04:43.649
like healthcare
and voter suppression,

00:04:43.649 --> 00:04:46.018
and it produced the largest
margin of victory

00:04:46.018 --> 00:04:47.219
in midterms history,

00:04:47.219 --> 00:04:49.588
so naturally Trump has responded
to that message

00:04:49.588 --> 00:04:51.757
with his only move -- racism.

00:04:51.757 --> 00:04:54.226
-2020 is also clearly
on President Trump's mind.

00:04:54.226 --> 00:04:56.929
Saturday, he lashed out at
Senator Warren on Twitter,

00:04:56.929 --> 00:04:59.665
alluding to her past claims
of Native American status,

00:04:59.665 --> 00:05:01.133
for which she has apologized.

00:05:01.133 --> 00:05:03.669
The President appeared
to make a joking reference

00:05:03.669 --> 00:05:06.672
to the tragic Trail of Tears
relocation and genocide

00:05:06.672 --> 00:05:08.040
of Native Americans.

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:11.811
-"Today, Elizabeth Warren,
sometimes referred to by me

00:05:11.811 --> 00:05:14.713
as Pocahontas,
joined the race for president.

00:05:14.713 --> 00:05:18.384
Will she run as our first Native
American presidential candidate,

00:05:18.384 --> 00:05:20.853
or has she decided that
after 32 years,

00:05:20.853 --> 00:05:23.156
this is not playing
so well anymore?

00:05:23.156 --> 00:05:25.324
See you on the campaign trail,
Liz."

00:05:25.324 --> 00:05:27.259
-Now, this tweet
was obviously racist,

00:05:27.259 --> 00:05:29.829
and yet there are actually
some conservatives arguing

00:05:29.829 --> 00:05:32.197
that it wasn't a reference to
the Trail of Tears

00:05:32.197 --> 00:05:34.200
because Trump doesn't know
what that is.

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:36.068
Fox News political analyst
Brit Hume

00:05:36.068 --> 00:05:38.471
responded to claims that Trump's
tweet was racist

00:05:38.471 --> 00:05:41.240
by saying yes, because Trump is
noted for his knowledge of

00:05:41.240 --> 00:05:44.210
19th century American history,
vis-a-vis the native population.

00:05:44.210 --> 00:05:46.011
They're actually defending Trump

00:05:46.011 --> 00:05:49.248
by saying he's too dumb
to be racist.

00:05:49.248 --> 00:05:51.417
First of all, if you ever find
yourself asking

00:05:51.417 --> 00:05:52.785
is Trump dumb or is he racist,

00:05:52.785 --> 00:05:55.687
the answer is most likely C --
all of the above.

00:05:55.687 --> 00:05:58.391
Second, Trump has said publicly
that he's a big fan

00:05:58.391 --> 00:05:59.759
of Andrew Jackson,

00:05:59.759 --> 00:06:02.294
who carried out the forced
removal and ethnic cleansing

00:06:02.294 --> 00:06:03.629
of Native Americans.

00:06:03.629 --> 00:06:06.165
In fact, early in his
presidency, Trump even claimed

00:06:06.165 --> 00:06:09.134
Jackson foresaw the Civil War
decades before it happened,

00:06:09.134 --> 00:06:11.404
although Trump didn't really
seem to have

00:06:11.404 --> 00:06:14.406
a strong understanding of what
the Civil War actually was.

00:06:14.406 --> 00:06:19.145
-They said my campaign is most
like my campaign and win,

00:06:19.145 --> 00:06:21.413
was most like Andrew Jackson.

00:06:21.413 --> 00:06:23.483
I mean, had Andrew Jackson
been a little bit later,

00:06:23.483 --> 00:06:25.017
you wouldn't have had
the Civil War.

00:06:25.017 --> 00:06:29.788
He was really angry
that he saw what was happening

00:06:29.788 --> 00:06:31.457
with regard to the Civil War.

00:06:31.457 --> 00:06:33.759
He said,
"There's no reason for this."

00:06:33.759 --> 00:06:38.397
People don't realize, you know,
the Civil War, um --

00:06:38.397 --> 00:06:39.965
-Yeah.

00:06:39.965 --> 00:06:41.900
-You think about it, why?

00:06:41.900 --> 00:06:43.803
People don't ask that question.

00:06:43.803 --> 00:06:45.737
But why was there the Civil War?

00:06:45.737 --> 00:06:48.508
Why could that one
not have been worked out?

00:06:48.508 --> 00:06:51.611
-What do you mean
why was there the Civil War?

00:06:51.611 --> 00:06:52.644
[ Laughter ]

00:06:52.644 --> 00:06:55.214
Everyone knows why.

00:06:55.214 --> 00:06:57.049
It's not like the first line of

00:06:57.049 --> 00:06:59.918
Abraham Lincoln's
Emancipation Proclamation was,

00:06:59.918 --> 00:07:01.888
"I don't know
why I'm doing this."

00:07:01.888 --> 00:07:03.856
[ Laughter ]

00:07:03.856 --> 00:07:06.391
Trump and his allies are
clearly rattled by the fact that

00:07:06.391 --> 00:07:08.727
for the first time
they have to face real questions

00:07:08.727 --> 00:07:10.596
from the Democrats
running for President

00:07:10.596 --> 00:07:12.264
or investigating them
in Congress.

00:07:12.264 --> 00:07:14.099
And there was no better example
of that

00:07:14.099 --> 00:07:16.468
than Trump's acting attorney
general, Matt Whitaker,

00:07:16.468 --> 00:07:19.171
who testified before the House
Judiciary Committee on Friday.

00:07:19.171 --> 00:07:21.707
Democrats tried to get Whitaker
to answer basic questions

00:07:21.707 --> 00:07:23.743
about his role
in the Russian investigation.

00:07:23.743 --> 00:07:26.478
And for the first time in any
congressional hearing in memory,

00:07:26.478 --> 00:07:29.648
the witness told them
that they were out of time.

00:07:29.648 --> 00:07:32.184
-In your capacity as
acting attorney general,

00:07:32.184 --> 00:07:35.154
have you ever been asked
to approve any request or action

00:07:35.154 --> 00:07:38.490
to be taken by
the special counsel?

00:07:38.490 --> 00:07:43.829
-Mr. Chairman, I see that your
five minutes is up, and so...

00:07:43.829 --> 00:07:47.399
-I'm sorry, but you don't get
to do that, dude.

00:07:47.399 --> 00:07:48.634
That's like Tom Brady

00:07:48.634 --> 00:07:51.470
chucking a flag
and calling pass interference.

00:07:51.470 --> 00:07:53.239
The way it works is Tom Brady

00:07:53.239 --> 00:07:55.908
winks at a ref
and the ref throws the flag.

00:07:55.908 --> 00:07:57.809
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:57.809 --> 00:08:00.479
This is what happens.

00:08:00.479 --> 00:08:02.481
This is what happens
when Trump and his allies

00:08:02.481 --> 00:08:04.850
finally have to answer real
questions for the first time

00:08:04.850 --> 00:08:07.019
from people that aren't just
there to protect them.

00:08:07.019 --> 00:08:09.087
Trump is dealing with several
serious challenges

00:08:09.087 --> 00:08:11.289
to his presidency and real
oversight from Congress.

00:08:11.289 --> 00:08:12.792
And by the time
this is all over,

00:08:12.792 --> 00:08:14.693
Trump may no longer be
the president of --

00:08:14.693 --> 00:08:16.628
-The United Shtates.

00:08:16.628 --> 00:08:17.963
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:08:17.963 --> 00:08:20.199
[ Cheers and applause ]

